{
  "id": "emergent-leader",
  "term": "emergent leader",
  "definition": "An emergent leader is a member of a pair or group who comes to take more of the guiding or predictive-control role as coordination unfolds, creating leader-follower movement dynamics without that role being set in advance. In joint action, this reflects how control becomes unevenly distributed between partners during co-regulation.",
